```{.r .cell-code}
r1 <- ctl |> filter(arm == "recon_automation")
r2 <- ctl |> filter(arm == "independent_pnl_verification")
```
:::


On expected loss alone, both controls are close to break-even: reconciliation automation saves $502.30K a year against a $400.00K cost (net $102.30K), and independent P&L verification saves $735.12K against $700.00K (net $35.12K). The tail benefit is larger: 95% expected shortfall of annual loss falls from $31.8M to $26.8M and $23.4M.


::: {.cell}

